  "layout": "standard d20: opposite faces sum to 21; high numbers spread apart (20 on face 0, each next high number on the free face farthest from the higher ones).",
  "reading": "the result is the face whose world normal points most UP: argmax_i dot(R * normal_i, (0,1,0)). (A d20 is read on the top face.)",
  "forcing_the_roll": "to land a given roll n without faking it: simulate once from q0, read the landed face m, then replay the SAME simulation from q0' = q0 * S^-1 where S = F_n * F_m^T (F = faces[i].frame, 3x3, columns = number-up, normal, right; body space). S is one of the icosahedron's 60 rotations, so the collision shape and the whole trajectory are identical and face n lands up.",
